1.30.0: polajuice curves - what a look does to color, charted

- 'polajuice curves -c CAMERA [look] -o NAME.svg [--vs FILM] [--table]':
  the look's color path run through a 33-point lattice and drawn four
  ways in one SVG - R, G, B against a gray ramp; hue turned and chroma
  scaled around the CIELAB hue circle; a color plane with an arrow from
  each color to where it goes; the 24 ColorChecker patches as numbers
  (dL, chroma %, hue degrees). --vs overlays the same look on another
  film (none = the scalar engine); --table prints the patch numbers,
  with or without -o. Readable without color vision: labelled, dashed
  lines, named hues, numbers.
- fix, found with it: --strength 0 was not the input on the scalar
  engine. The tone curve's parameters were blended toward a roll-off of
  1, which is still a shoulder (a red patch came out 17% more
  saturated at strength 0). The curve is now applied at full strength
  and blended with the input. Strength 1 is unchanged to the bit;
  renders at strengths between 0 and 1 without a film LUT change
  slightly.

Tests: compat (SVG structure, table, identity at strength 0, --vs,
-o or --table required).
Docs: README, man page, completions.
